  "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of hyperboloids of one sheet:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\\,c\\in (0,\\infty ).\n$$",
